From 6ec77446eb1d42f5b73ae2f162faf8975e439320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:58:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45 becomes Freeciv45: stacks of units on a square map,
 only the defender dies

The one-unit-per-tile rules move out (they live on in civ54): sandbox's
Unit Move and Transport Disembark enablers come back, the StacksAnywhere
and StacksInPort flags and the relocation Lua go. New games default to
an overhead square map (topology "") that wraps east to west, with
killstack disabled, so a stack that loses its defender loses only that
unit. The culture steps on the city radius go too: on a square map
radius_sq 5 is the 21-tile fat cross. The ruleset is named "Freeciv45",
suggests the trident tileset (the only overhead square one shipped) and
its Makefile.am names civ45 instead of sandbox.
---
 data/civ45/Makefile.am     |   4 +-
 data/civ45/README.civ45    |  49 ++++-----
 data/civ45/actions.ruleset |  78 --------------
 data/civ45/effects.ruleset |  19 ----
 data/civ45/game.ruleset    |  29 ++---
 data/civ45/script.lua      | 212 -------------------------------------
 data/civ45/units.ruleset   |  48 ++++-----
 7 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 374 deletions(-)

