index e2bb068..01fe760 100644
--- a/data/civ45/README.civ45
+++ b/data/civ45/README.civ45
@@ -1,35 +1,32 @@
-=============
-Civ45 Ruleset
-=============
+=================
+Freeciv45 Ruleset
+=================
 
-civ45 is the sandbox ruleset plus a first slice of Civilization IV/V
-style rules. It is part of the freeciv-macos27 project
+civ45 is the ruleset of Freeciv45, an empire game where units travel in
+stacks on a square map. It is the sandbox ruleset plus the rules below.
+It is part of the freeciv-macos27 project
 (https://github.com/John-ODell/freeciv-macos27) and is experimental:
-balance is untuned and the default AI was not written for one unit per
-tile.
+balance is untuned.
+
+The one-unit-per-tile hex rules this ruleset had in its first two slices
+live on unchanged as the civ54 ruleset.
 
 Differences from sandbox
 ------------------------
 
-- Hex map (topology ISO|HEX) by default.
-- One unit per tile, cities included:
-  * A regular move or a landing from a transport is only legal into an
-    empty tile (MaxUnitsOnTile 0 on the "Unit Move" and "Transport
-    Disembark" enablers).
-  * A unit built in a city that already holds a unit is sorted out at
-    once by script.lua: the better defender stays in the city, the other
-    unit moves to the nearest free tile in its owner's territory.
-  * Every turn starts with a sweep that does the same for any other way
-    two units ended up together (start units, huts, barbarians, captures,
-    airlifts, paradrops, unloading in port).
-  * Exempt: units inside a transport; aircraft, helicopters and missiles
-    (unit flag "StacksAnywhere"), which may share any tile; ships (unit
-    flag "StacksInPort"), which may enter and share a city tile.
-  * Known limit: the move rule counts every unit, so a ship or aircraft
-    parked in a city stops a land unit from moving in. Units built there
-    still appear inside.
-- City work radius grows with the city's culture: +4 radius_sq at 300
-  culture points, another +4 at 1500.
+- Stacks: any number of units can share a tile, as in sandbox. When a
+  stack is attacked its best defender fights, and if it loses, only that
+  unit dies (server setting killstack disabled; sandbox kills the whole
+  stack outside cities and fortresses).
+- Square map seen from above (topology "", overhead tilesets such as
+  trident) that wraps east to west only (wrap WRAPX), instead of
+  sandbox's isometric map wrapping both ways.
+- Each city works 21 tiles: radius_sq 5 on a square map, the "fat cross"
+  shape. Earlier slices grew the radius with culture; that is gone (on a
+  square map it would reach 29 and then 45 tiles). Sandbox's Space
+  Elevator and Space Elevator Tether still enlarge their own city's radius.
+- The ruleset suggests the trident tileset, the only overhead square
+  tileset Freeciv ships, until a Freeciv45 tileset exists.
 - Cultural victory is enabled alongside spacerace and allied victory.
 - Bombard range is 2 instead of 1.
 - Strategic resources: Legion needs Iron and Armor needs Oil somewhere in
